Both tight configs at n=14 -- AP {1..13} and Goddyn-Wong {1..11,13,24} -- have M=1/14 achieved at IDENTICAL witnesses:
  t = a/14 for a in units mod 14 = {1,3,5,9,11,13} = Phi_14 (the primitive 14th roots), all with M=1/14 EXACT.
  3 antipodal pairs (1,13),(3,11),(5,9); binders at t=a/14 are {+-a^{-1} mod 14} = the antipodal pair.
The witnesses are determined by the SHARED small residues {1..11,13} mod 14 (GW's 24=10 mod14 is never a binder).
=> mac-mini's Vitali CORE construction (HYP-3237) is UNIFORM across the tight locus, not AP-specific; the
   Borsuk-Ulam index 3 (= (p-1)/2, HYP-3241) and the equioscillation are config-independent on the core.
